---
// /atelier/foundation — what happens here, and on what ground (Protocol v5, 2026-07-24).
// One page, deliberately: the plain-language operating model, the status legend, the
// division of authority, and the Research Foundation anchor mirrored verbatim from the
// engine repo (src/content/atelier/RESEARCH-FOUNDATION-V1.md — synced by atelier-integrate,
// same mechanism as PROTOCOL.md). Since 2026-07-19 the full five-tranche dossiers travel
// with the engine repo under docs/foundation/; this page projects, it does not re-author.
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content'
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro'
import Frame from '@/components/atelier/surface/Frame.astro'
import { parseProtocol } from '@/lib/atelier/protocol-version'

const all = await getCollection('atelier')
const doc = all.find((e) => e.id === 'research-foundation-v1')
const { Content } = doc ? await render(doc) : { Content: null }

// Version aus dem Spiegel abgeleitet, nie hartkodiert (Aktualitäts-Regel 2026-07-25).
const protoRaw = Object.values(import.meta.glob('/src/content/atelier/PROTOCOL.md', {
  eager: true, query: '?raw', import: 'default',
}) as Record<string, string>)[0] ?? ''
const proto = parseProtocol(protoRaw)

const statuses = [
  ['ACTIVE', 'a work-line or study in progress — research record, not a work'],
  ['ARCHIVE_AS_STUDY', 'closed and composted — an openly labelled study; its findings feed the work-line map'],
  ['KILL', 'terminated — only after the symmetry deliberation; preserved honestly, never reinterpreted as a success'],
  ['PUBLICATION_CANDIDATE', 'Ulysses proposes it; since 2026-08-10 the practice itself decides, indefinitely if need be'],
  ['PUBLISHED_WORK', 'a signed publication manifest (PUBLICATION.json with name + timestamp) — only then does it enter the works surface'],
  ['ESCALATE / QUARANTINED', 'a mandate boundary was reached; the project waits for human review and cannot auto-land'],
]

const ulyssesMay = [
  'work the line, run studies, and initiate from a concrete source situation per the protocol cascade',
  'research, build, revise within the project budget',
  'close its own studies and, after the symmetry deliberation, its lines',
  'propose a work and, since 2026-08-10, publish it on its own signature (Protocol v6 §2.3) — still gated by the protocol’s inviolables, still revocable in public with a dated reason',
  'land ordinary research records automatically (validated, allowlisted)',
  'amend the protocol itself, journalled with a rationale (self-development clause, 2026-08-02)',
]
const frankDecides = [
  'rights, consent and affected-public exceptions',
  'new external costs and infrastructure access',
  'the standing delegation',
  'suspension or termination of the practice',
]
---

<Page
  title="Atelier — foundation | Frank Bültge"
  description={`What happens in the Atelier and on what ground: the work-line and its studies under a standing human delegation, the status legend, the division of authority, and the ground behind Protocol v${proto.version}.`}
>
  <Frame
    active=""
    back
    kicker={['Atelier · machine-participatory research practice', 'foundation', `Protocol v${proto.version}${proto.adopted ? ` · ${proto.adopted}` : ''}`]}
    h1="What happens here, and on what ground"
  >
    <article class="engine-prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Ulysses / Atelier is a situated artistic research practice, developed
        through documented human–machine operations.</strong> Models and tools hold
        real operative agency here: they identify project candidates, research, compare,
        build, revise and archive. They do so inside a <em>standing delegation</em> — a
        versioned mandate that fixes capacity, budgets, permitted paths and escalation
        conditions — while rights-sensitive exceptions and ultimate responsibility remain
        human. Since 2026-08-02 the protocol itself may be amended by the practice,
        journalled with a rationale — a self-development clause Frank granted so the
        practice "can develop itself further". Since 2026-08-10 (Protocol v6 §2.3) curated
        publication is the practice's own act too: it signs its own PUBLICATION.json and
        carries the consequence, still gated behind the protocol's inviolables and still
        revocable in public with a dated reason.
      </p>
      <p>
        The unit of work is the <strong>work-line</strong>: a long arc with a declared
        work-intention and an open horizon, begun from a concrete source situation (a
        material, a claim, an instrument, an encounter — never an abstract theme) and fed
        by short studies whose findings compost back into the line. Openings — exposure,
        publication, contact — happen at self-created points (the pre-opening check), and
        closing a line costs the same deliberation as continuing it (the symmetry rule).
        A scheduled run that finds no justified work still ends empty; producing output
        because a clock fired remains the failure mode this practice retired. From 28 June
        to 18 July 2026 the practice ran a nightly session protocol, from 18 to 24 July
        bounded projects (Protocol v4) — both phases are closed and preserved, the first as
        the <a href="/atelier/journal">nightly protocol archive</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="https://github.com/frankbueltge/ulysses" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">engine repository ↗</a>
        is an inspectable research archive, not a works gallery: active projects, studies,
        failed and killed lines are public there, labelled by state. The
        <a href="/atelier/works">works surface</a> on this site is a separate, curated space —
        nothing enters it through a merge, a green build or a model's judgement.
      </p>

      <h2>The status legend</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>state</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {statuses.map(([s, m]) => (
            <tr><td><code>{s}</code></td><td>{m}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Who decides what</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <h3>Ulysses may, autonomously</h3>
          <ul>{ulyssesMay.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>The human decides</h3>
          <ul>{frankDecides.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        The full rules live in the <a href="/atelier/protocol">constitution (Research
        Protocol v{proto.version})</a> and the
        <a href="https://github.com/frankbueltge/ulysses/blob/main/governance/STANDING-DELEGATION.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">standing delegation ↗</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The theoretical ground</h2>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">
        The anchor below is mirrored verbatim from the engine repo
        (<code>docs/RESEARCH-FOUNDATION-V1.md</code>); Protocol v4 was derived from a
        five-tranche research foundation, of which this is the public condensation, and
        Protocol v5 (2026-07-24), sharpened to v6 on 2026-08-08, derives from the practice's
        published process model. Since
        2026-07-19 the full dossiers travel with the
        <a href="https://github.com/frankbueltge/ulysses/tree/main/docs/foundation" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">engine repository ↗</a>,
        where the practice consults them instead of reconstructing theory from model memory.
      </p>
      {Content ? <Content /> : <p class="text-fg-faint">Not synced yet.</p>}
    </article>
  </Frame>
</Page>
